  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 356 AM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nThe mid/upper ridge has shifted eastward toward the Ohio Valley area \nas a WSW jet streak extends from the Central Great Basin/Central \nRockies  ENE into the Central and Northern Plains. This may allow a \nsubtle decrease in temperatures across the area today but it will \nlikely be offset by a subtle increase in low level moisture leading \nto higher heat indices and a Heat Advisory is now in effect for much \nof the area through Friday. Low level southerly flow will gradually \nadvect higher dewpoints into the area today and especially on \nThursday-Friday. Deep mixing within the pbl may mix out some of this \nmoisture, especially in parts of central and south central KS but a \nsteady increase in low level moisture is still anticipated as we \nmove into Thu-Fri. This will drive heat indices into the 105-108 \nrange for many areas. The mid/upper ridge is still progged to \namplify as we move into Fri-Sun periods while remaining draped \nacross the region into the middle of next week. This will result in \na continuation of much above normal temperatures across the area \nthis weekend and persisting into at least the middle of next week \nbefore we see a pattern change. Some record high/record warm minimum \ntemperatures may be possible at times through the upcoming week. \nChances for meaningful precipitation are also expected to \nremain low through the upcoming week.",
